  "Monolith Soft 官方社长访谈确认公司于 2007 年通过股权转让成为任天堂子公司，并把 2010 年《异度神剑》列为其后获得用户认可的作品；任天堂官方财务资料确认发售时间。": "An official interview with Monolith Soft's president confirmed that the company became a Nintendo subsidiary through equity transfer in 2007, and listed Xenoblade from 2010 as a title that later gained user recognition; Nintendo's official financial data confirms the release date.",
  "Monolith Soft 于 2007 年通过股权转让进入任天堂集团；2010 年发行的 Xenoblade Chronicles，是本时间线中此后最先推出的 Xeno 作品。Monolith Soft 官方回顾把加入任天堂与后续创作条件改善直接联系起来，但这里仍只把本作视为新组织关系下的首个谱系作品，不把所有设计成果简单归因于收购。": "Monolith Soft joined the Nintendo Group in 2007 through a share transfer; Released in 2010, Xenoblade Chronicles was the first Xeno title to be released in this timeline after that. The official Monolith Soft retrospective directly links joining Nintendo with improvements in subsequent creative conditions, but here it is still considered only the first lineage title under the new organizational relationship, without simply attributing all design achievements to acquisitions.",
  "Moonlighting 允许角色同时调用两个已培养职业的能力，减少频繁换职造成的功能断裂；石板提示、场景精简与战斗加速共同压缩原版长前序和重复移动。": "Moonlighting allows characters to simultaneously call the abilities of two cultivated jobs, reducing functional breaks caused by frequent job changes; Slate hints, scene streamlining, and battle acceleration all compress the long prelude and repetitive movement of the original.",
  "N64 的磁碟扩展，商业规模很小，但 Mario Artist、Doshin 和 Randnet 体现了任天堂的内容创作与联网实验。": "The N64's disk expansion was small in scale, but Mario Artist, Doshin, and Randnet embodyed Nintendo's content creation and networking experiments.",
  "Namco 的发行公告将本作记录为首款采用单面双层 DVD-ROM 的 PS2 软件；它用更大介质容量避免游戏中换盘，以支撑当时罕见的大量语音与长篇过场，是主机 RPG 以光盘容量服务电影化叙事的具体技术案例。": "Namco's release announcement recorded this as the first PS2 software to use a single-sided, double-layer DVD-ROM; It uses larger media capacity to avoid disc switching during games, supporting the rare volume of voice lines and long cutscenes at the time. It is a concrete example of console RPGs using CD capacity to serve cinematic storytelling.",
